## Why This Is Asked
Assesses practical, beginner-friendly encryption practices that map to real-world apps without backend changes.

## Key Concepts
- Encryption at rest with AES-GCM
- Password-based key derivation (Argon2id)
- OS-level key storage (Keychain/Keystore)
- Key rotation and re-encryption on login

## Code Example
```javascript
// Derive key from password and encrypt a note (simplified)
const crypto = require('crypto');
function deriveKey(password, salt) {
  // Argon2id in real code; use placeholder PBKDF2 for illustration
  return crypto.pbkdf2Sync(password, salt, 100000, 32, 'sha256');
}
function encryptNote(key, plaintext) {
  const iv = crypto.randomBytes(12);
  const cipher = crypto.createCipheriv('aes-256-gcm', key, iv);
  const enc = Buffer.concat([cipher.update(plaintext, 'utf8'), cipher.final()]);
  const tag = cipher.getAuthTag();
  return { iv: iv.toString('hex'), data: enc.toString('hex'), tag: tag.toString('hex') };
}
```

